  "$comment": "THE single editable source for EVERYTHING about plans — the billing numbers AND the marketing copy. Two consumers read this file: (1) billing (src/lib/billing/catalog.ts + scripts/sync-billing.mjs) uses plans[].{key,name,blurb,listed,sort,includedMonthlyCredits,overage,entitlements}, prices, creditPacks, creditRates — `npm run billing:sync` publishes them to the DB (append-only: an entitlement/credit change mints a NEW immutable plan version so existing subscriptions stay pinned to what they bought — legacy vs new is automatic — and prices are archived, never mutated); `npm run billing:publish` mirrors them to Stripe. (2) marketing (src/lib/billing/plan-content.ts) uses plans[].display, positioning, and matrix for the /pricing page and the in-app Settings→Billing surface. IMPORTANT: display/matrix/positioning are DISPLAY-ONLY — editing them does NOT mint a new billing plan version (a bullet-wording change must not reprice anyone). Price strings on the cards are DERIVED from prices[] (not stored here), so a price change updates the cards automatically. A unit test (billing-plan-content.test.ts) fails if the matrix's numeric/flag claims disagree with entitlements, so the copy can't silently drift from what's enforced. Money is integer cents; credits are integers.",
